module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraSheafModuleFunctor.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ColimitGlobal.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.Basic
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Sections of a quasi-coherent algebra lie in a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra

Let `X` be a scheme and `A` a quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras. The affine
sections statement that the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] is reduced to by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections`
asks that **every**
section of `A` over **every** affine open come from a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra of
`A`. `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag05JTColimitGlobal.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_top`
proves it at the open `⊤`.

The content of this file is that the statement at an affine open `V` **implies** the statement
at every affine open `U ≤ V`: a section over `U` is a `Γ(X, U)`-linear combination of
restrictions of finitely many sections over `V`, each of those lies in a finite type
quasi-coherent subalgebra, finitely many such subalgebras are dominated by a single one because
they are filtered, and the sections over `U` coming from a fixed subalgebra form a
`Γ(X, U)`-submodule. In particular, on an **affine** scheme the statement at `⊤` already gives
the statement at every affine open, so the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] holds there.

The direction of this implication is worth noticing: sheaf-theoretic hypotheses usually descend
to *smaller* opens, and here the hypothesis is inherited from a *larger* affine open. That is
what makes an affine scheme a complete case rather than a first step — `⊤` is then affine and
dominates every open — and it is also why the general case is not reducible to a finite affine
covering by this argument: an arbitrary affine open of a general scheme need not be contained in
a member of a chosen covering.

## Main results

* `exists_preimage_of_mem_span`: a purely module-level statement, and the reusable core. If
  `φ : M ⟶ N` is a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules, `U ≤ V`, and a section of `N` over `U` lies in the
  `Γ(X, U)`-span of the restrictions of sections of `N` over `V` that are in the image of `φ`,
  then it is itself in the image of `φ`.
* `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_of_finite`: finitely many sections of `A` over an open, each
  coming from some finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra, all come from a **single** one. This
  is where filteredness of the subalgebras is used, through
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra`.
* `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_le`: the affine sections statement at an affine open
  `V` implies it at every affine open `U ≤ V`.
* `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine`: on an affine scheme, every section of `A`
  over every affine open comes from a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra — the affine
  sections statement in full, with **no finite type hypothesis on `A`**.
* `nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_of_isAffine`: **the colimit assertion of
  [Stacks, Tag 05JT] for an affine scheme.**

## Why no stacks attribute is attached here

No stacks attribute is attached, because what is proved here carries `IsAffine X` while the
colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] is stated for a quasi-compact and quasi-separated
scheme. That assertion is proved in that generality as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered`'s
`nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone`, which carries the attribute, and the
corresponding assertion of part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0817] is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteSubalgebras.nonempty_isColimit_finiteSubalgebraCocone`.

The extension step those need — for `V` an affine open of a quasi-compact quasi-separated `X` and
`x` a section of `A` over `V`, a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra of `A` on the whole of `X`
having `x` among its sections over `V` — is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section`. It
*is* a reduction to the module statement of [Stacks, Tag 01PF]: the passage from a finite type
quasi-coherent submodule to a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.genSubalg`, the subalgebra generated by the
submodule, and it needs no symmetric algebra.

## Implementation notes

The three spellings of the sections of an algebra sheaf over an open — the ring
`A.right.obj.obj (op U)`, the module `Γ(Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U)`
and `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.sections A U` — are definitionally equal, and so are the
restriction maps and the maps induced by a morphism of algebra sheaves: every passage
between them below is `rfl` or an `exact` against a defeq goal. What is *not* interchangeable is
which `Module Γ(X, U)` instance a `Submodule Γ(X, U)` is formed over, so every statement that
mentions a span or a linear map is phrased at the module spelling, which is the one carrying
Mathlib's `Scheme.Modules` instance, and `exists_preimage_of_mem_span` is stated for a morphism
of `𝒪_X`-modules rather than for the arrow of a subalgebra. The morphism of underlying modules
induced by a morphism of algebra sheaves is
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModuleFunctor`, whose sections are the sections of
the morphism of sheaves of rings by `rfl`.

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.exists_finite_subset_span` is the only input that needs
affineness, and it needs it for both opens: it is the surjectivity half of [Stacks, Tag 01I9],
that the sections of a quasi-coherent module over an affine open are generated by the
restrictions of the sections over a larger affine open. No finiteness of `A` is involved, since
only one section at a time is being written as a combination; that is why the hypothesis of the
module-level affine case of [Stacks, Tag 01PF] — finiteness of the sections over the affine
opens of `W` — has no counterpart here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.RelativeSpec

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraAffineSections

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebras

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### The image of a morphism of modules is a submodule, compatibly with restriction -/

/-- **The sections over `U` in the image of a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules form a
`Γ(X, U)`-submodule containing the restrictions of the sections over `V` in its image.** So a
section of `N` over `U` which is a `Γ(X, U)`-combination of restrictions of sections of `N` over
`V` lying in the image of `φ` lies in the image of `φ` itself.

This is the one step of the argument that is about modules rather than algebras: the image of a
morphism of *algebra* sheaves is closed under addition and multiplication but not under
multiplication by sections of `𝒪_X`, while the image of the induced morphism of underlying
modules is, and that is what a span needs. No hypothesis on `X`, on `U`, on `V` or on the
modules is used. -/
theorem exists_preimage_of_mem_span {M N : X.Modules} (φ : M ⟶ N) {U V : X.Opens} (hUV : U ≤ V)
    {s : Set Γ(N, V)} (hs : ∀ m ∈ s, ∃ y : Γ(M, V), φ.app V y = m) {x : Γ(N, U)}
    (hx : x ∈ Submodule.span Γ(X, U) (N.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUV).op '' s)) :
    ∃ y : Γ(M, U), φ.app U y = x := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem z hz =>
      obtain ⟨m, hm, rfl⟩ := hz
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hs m hm
      refine ⟨M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUV).op y, ?_⟩
      rw [← hy]
      exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (φ.mapPresheaf.naturality (homOfLE hUV).op) y
  | zero => exact ⟨0, map_zero _⟩
  | add a b _ _ ha hb =>
      obtain ⟨ya, hya⟩ := ha
      obtain ⟨yb, hyb⟩ := hb
      exact ⟨ya + yb, by rw [map_add, hya, hyb]⟩
  | smul r a _ ha =>
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := ha
      exact ⟨r • y, by rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul, hy]⟩

/-! ### Finitely many sections lie in a single finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra -/

/-- **A section coming from a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra comes from any larger
one.** The witness is the image of the given one under the morphism of subobjects, and the
identity it satisfies is `CategoryTheory.Subobject.underlying_arrow` read on sections. -/
theorem exists_section_of_hom {A : AlgebraSheaf X} {B C : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A} (f : B ⟶ C)
    (U : X.Opens) {x : A.right.obj.obj (op U)}
    (h : ∃ y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U),
      B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = x) :
    ∃ z : (C.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U),
      C.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) z = x := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := h
  refine ⟨(Subobject.underlying.map f.hom).right.hom.app (op U) y, Eq.trans ?_ hy⟩
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (congrArg (fun g : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X) ⟶ A => g.right.hom.app (op U))
      (Subobject.underlying_arrow f.hom)) y

/-- **Finitely many sections of `A` over an open, each coming from some finite type
quasi-coherent subalgebra of `A`, all come from a single one.** Induction on the finite set:
the empty set is handled by any object at all, and the induction step by the binary upper bound
of the filtered category `FiniteTypeSubalgebra A`.

Filteredness is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra` and is
unconditional, so the only hypothesis is the quasi-coherence of `A`. The open `U` is
arbitrary. -/
theorem exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_of_finite (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) {U : X.Opens} {s : Set (A.right.obj.obj (op U))}
    (hs : s.Finite)
    (hmem : ∀ m ∈ s, ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A)
      (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
        B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = m) :
    ∃ B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A, ∀ m ∈ s,
      ∃ y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U),
        B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = m := by
  let _ := FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra A hA
  induction s, hs using Set.Finite.induction_on with
  | empty => exact ⟨IsFiltered.nonempty.some, by simp⟩
  | @insert a s ha hsfin ih =>
      obtain ⟨B, hB⟩ := ih fun m hm => hmem m (Set.mem_insert_of_mem a hm)
      obtain ⟨B', y', hy'⟩ := hmem a (Set.mem_insert a s)
      refine ⟨IsFiltered.max B B', fun m hm => ?_⟩
      rcases hm with hm | hm
      · exact exists_section_of_hom (IsFiltered.rightToMax B B') U ⟨y', hm ▸ hy'⟩
      · exact exists_section_of_hom (IsFiltered.leftToMax B B') U (hB m hm)

/-! ### From an affine open to the affine opens inside it -/

/-- **The affine sections statement at an affine open `V` implies it at every affine open
`U ≤ V`.** If every section of `A` over `V` comes from a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra
of `A`, then so does every section of `A` over any affine open `U ≤ V`.

The section over `U` is a `Γ(X, U)`-combination of restrictions of finitely many sections over
`V` by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.exists_finite_subset_span`; those finitely many
come from a single finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra by
`exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_of_finite`; and the sections over `U` coming from that one
subalgebra form a `Γ(X, U)`-submodule by `exists_preimage_of_mem_span`. -/
theorem exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_le (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) {U V : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (hUV : U ≤ V)
    (hsec : ∀ m : A.right.obj.obj (op V), ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A)
      (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op V)),
        B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op V) y = m)
    (x : A.right.obj.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
      B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = x := by
  have := hA
  obtain ⟨s, hsfin, hspan⟩ := GabberColimit.exists_finite_subset_span
    (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A) ⟨V, hV⟩ ⟨U, hU⟩ x
  obtain ⟨B, hB⟩ := exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_of_finite A hA (U := V) (s := s) hsfin
    fun m hm => hsec m
  exact ⟨B, exists_preimage_of_mem_span
    ((AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModuleFunctor X).map B.obj.arrow) hUV hB (hspan hUV)⟩

/-- **The affine sections statement on an affine scheme.** Let `X` be an affine scheme and `A` a
quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras. Every section of `A` over every affine open
of `X` comes from a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra of `A`.

This is `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_le` at `V = ⊤`, whose hypothesis is then
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag05JTColimitGlobal.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_top`. No
finite type hypothesis on `A` is needed. -/
theorem exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine [IsAffine X] (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (x : A.right.obj.obj (op U)) :
    ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebra A) (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op U)),
      B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op U) y = x :=
  exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_le A hA hU (isAffineOpen_top X) le_top
    (fun m => Tag05JTColimitGlobal.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_top A hA m) x

/-- **The colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] for an affine scheme.** A quasi-coherent sheaf
of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras on an affine scheme is the colimit of its finite type
quasi-coherent subalgebras, with the canonical inclusions.

No attribute is attached here: the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] is stated for a
quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme, `IsAffine X` is a hypothesis it does not grant, and the
attribute sits on the statement in that generality,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered`'s
`nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone`. This declaration is kept because it goes
through the affine-scheme sections statement above, which needs no [Stacks, Tag 01PF]. -/
@[ega "I 9.6.6" "special case"]
theorem nonempty_isColimit_finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone_of_isAffine [IsAffine X]
    (A : AlgebraSheaf X) (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteTypeSubalgebraCocone A)) :=
  FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections A hA
    fun _ hU x => exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_isAffine A hA hU x

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraAffineSections

end
